  "limitations": [
    "Cooperative same-UID local process/disk proof only; no native DAC/VM isolation or independent rollback domain certification.",
    "Issuer full source validation and persistent issuer/provider services remain C3b-3; unit tests inject signed public issuer evidence.",
    "Barrier transitions use explicitly injected cooperative drained proofs; actual service drain, manager stop and external-effect fencing remain C3b-4/C3d.",
    "C2 client/outcome mapping, RecordUse, consumer ACK, whole-path throughput/budget and shutdown integration remain C3b-5.",
    "Stage history is bounded: ordinary work stops with capacity_exhausted when 16 stages or 20,000 record bytes remain (20 pin cycles were observed from a new lineage), which keeps two full restart cycles; a further restart is refused and long-running GC/compaction is not implemented.",
    "Anchor minimum is supplied independently by the root application; a same-host minimum does not prove external rollback protection.",
    "Process storage faults are injected at real disk publication phases, not physical power-loss or hardware-failure certification.",
    "aux.AbandonEnrollment cannot be resolved through control.QueryOperation because its originalAPI enum is the C0 schema; after an unknown result the lineage phase is read through aux.ReadContext.",
    "Latency figures are one local run with no wall-clock guarantee; the 5 s budget under load and on other storage remains C3d work."
  ],
  "reviewFix": {
    "baseCommit": "acacac7",
    "rootCauses": [
      "prepareOwnerSignature decoded bodies with the 16 KiB frame default, so the signed anchor.cas request failed once a record passed about 12 KiB, after the record was saved; the registry blocked at revision 8 and restart repeated the failure",
      "Every stage image repeated all earlier records, and each history replay ran a ledger-wide check per row and rewrote and synced every file, so a write exceeded the 5 s deadline at about revision 10",
      "After saving a record the commit path rechecked the caller, so one expired, revoked or disconnected request blocked the registry for every peer",
      "CheckLiveBinding returned its reply without await, so admission was cleared first and the API could not succeed; provision targets were also refused by the serving check",
      "Concurrent requests were refused as busy instead of being served in order"
    ],
    "contract": [
      "Everything that could refuse a record later (stage count and exact signed anchor.cas size) is checked before saving; a refusal is capacity_exhausted and does not block",
      "Ordinary work keeps 16 stages and 20,000 record bytes for restart invalidation and barrier maintenance",
      "Once a record is saved, adoption completes using only the owner's own state; a caller failure affects only its reply and the result stays in the ledger",
      "Each stage image stores one record; the chain is rebuilt from verified history",
      "Full file resync runs at recovery; a request replays authenticated history and refuses an unresolved tail",
      "Requests are served in arrival order with at most 64 waiting",
      "A local refusal that sent nothing leaves a business request re-runnable"
    ],
